{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1902","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Binary Imbalance"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a string $$$s$$$, consisting only of characters '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' and/or '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one operation, you choose a position $$$i$$$ from $$$1$$$ to $$$|s| - 1$$$, where $$$|s|$$$ is the current length of string $$$s$$$. Then you insert a character between the $$$i$$$-th and the $$$(i+1)$$$-st characters of $$$s$$$. If $$$s_i = s_{i+1}$$$, you insert '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'. If $$$s_i \\neq s_{i+1}$$$, you insert '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Is it possible to make the number of zeroes in the string strictly greater than the number of ones, using any number of operations (possibly, none)?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 100$$$) — the number of testcases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each testcase contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 100$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains a string $$$s$$$ of length exactly $$$n$$$, consisting only of characters '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' and/or '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each testcase, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if it's possible to make the number of zeroes in $$$s$$$ strictly greater than the number of ones, using any number of operations (possibly, none). Otherwise, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n2\n00\n2\n11\n2\n10\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nNO\nYES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first testcase, the number of zeroes is already greater than the number of ones."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second testcase, it's impossible to insert any zeroes in the string."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third testcase, you can choose $$$i = 1$$$ to insert a zero between the $$$1$$$-st and the $$$2$$$-nd characters. Since $$$s_1 \\neq s_2$$$, you insert a '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'. The resulting string is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"100"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". It has two zeroes and only a single one, so the answer is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1902A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1902/problem/A"}